{
  // Config for `svelte-package --tsconfig` ONLY (see the "build" script). It exists
  // because svelte-package's own `.svelte.d.ts` emission (svelte2tsx's `emitDts`, run
  // through a throwaway "shadow" TypeScript program over the transformed `.svelte`
  // sources) silently emits NOTHING under this package's real `tsconfig.json` — no
  // error, no output file, no message — and two settings are involved, verified by
  // toggling each alone against the real `svelte-package -i src/lib -o <dir>
  // --tsconfig <probe>` invocation:
  //
  // 1. `noEmitOnError: true` (inherited from the repo base tsconfig) is the actual
  //    cause: with ONLY this relaxed to `false` (composite left at its inherited
  //    `true`), `svelte-package` emits the full set — AparteChat.svelte.d.ts,
  //    AparteUi.svelte.d.ts, index.d.ts, types.d.ts, stores/*.d.ts — byte-identical
  //    to this package's committed dist (bar the sourcemap URL). The block is
  //    diagnostics that are EXPECTED in svelte2tsx's `dts` transform mode: the
  //    generated code references helper identifiers (`svelteHTML`,
  //    `__sveltets_createSlot`) that this shadow program's ambient shim does not
  //    declare, and a `.svelte` file with an unread top-level const reads as unused.
  //    svelte2tsx's OWN "likely failed" filter (the diagnostic codes it treats as
  //    real generation failures — 2527, 5088, 2742, 9005-9039, 4000-4108) already
  //    excludes exactly these codes (2304 "cannot find name", 2454 "used before
  //    being assigned", 6133 "declared but never read") as known noise for this
  //    mode. `noEmitOnError: false` here matches that upstream judgment: the .d.ts
  //    SHAPE still comes out correct (verified against a consumer `tsc --noEmit`),
  //    only the shadow program's internal diagnostics are irrelevant.
  // 2. `composite` is NOT a cause, in either direction — verified the same way: with
  //    ONLY `composite: false` (noEmitOnError left at its inherited `true`),
  //    `svelte-package` still emits nothing. It is left at its inherited `true`
  //    here; there is nothing to override.
  //
  // `declarationMap: false`: svelte2tsx's own sourcemap-source rewrite (mapping the
  // virtual `AparteChat.svelte.ts` back to the real `.svelte` file) did not fire for
  // this program shape — the emitted `.d.ts.map`'s `sources` field names
  // `AparteChat.svelte.ts`, a file that does not exist on disk (the real file is
  // `AparteChat.svelte`), confirmed by reading the emitted map directly. That is
  // worse for an IDE's "go to definition" than no map at all. Off until that
  // resolves upstream.
  //
  // Neither override reaches the real build: `tsc -b --emitDeclarationOnly` for this
  // package's own `.ts` sources still runs against `tsconfig.json` unmodified, with
  // both `composite` and `noEmitOnError` at their strict repo defaults.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "declarationMap": false,
    "noEmitOnError": false
  }
}
